      "writtenOn": "2025-09-02T06:44:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would say that current code is simple enough to see that nalloc is ended every time and it feels a bit artificial to construct a C++ object just to run C functions that act on global values.\n\nWe could also have `nalloc_start` later (after WebPAnimDecoderNew), what do you think ? (to focus on WebPAnimDecoderGetNext and not on WebPGetFeatures)\n\nSide note : `nalloc_init` can be called only once per the lifetime of the program (like per `LLVMFuzzerInitialize`), when `nalloc_start` needs to be called for every input.",
      "parentUuid": "4b1dcdbc_9f74699d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
